Z||000012||Fret Naught||05-06-2000||12:22 PM||||No, the paint is not original, when I went looking for a Fiero I had my heart set on a Red one, (same color as my mom's) but after test driving lots of cars, when I drove this one, and saw how good of shape it was in color didn't matter. Paid 2K. The color is sometimes blue sometimes purple it depends on the lighting. I did manage to find out the brand name of paint Deltron PPG 2000 and the color # DBC 4982. I went to a PPG supplier and got the mix codes lots of pearl and flake in it. The whole thing was painted trim and all. I pulled all the trim and painted it black. The bra covers a multitude of sins. I have toyed with repainting the hood and nosecone, but am real leary. I have never sprayed BC/CC and don't know how good the match would turn out. If any one has advice on that topic. I will listen UP! Thanks again, all these nice comments are good for my ego.||||reg||6
